{"title":"Career Roadmap · Supply Chain Executive","role":"Supply Chain Executive","summary":"A Supply Chain Executive coordinates the flow of materials, information, inventory, and finished products from suppliers through production and distribution to customers.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Industrial Engineering & Management"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Supply Chain Executive coordinates the flow of materials, information, inventory, and finished products from suppliers through production and distribution to customers."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Industrial Engineering & Management graduate, this is a strong fit because the degree combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial engineering"},{"text":"Operations management"},{"text":"Production planning"},{"text":"Inventory management"},{"text":"Logistics"},{"text":"Supply chain management"},{"text":"Operations research"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Process optimization"},{"text":"Cost and productivity management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The modern role is increasingly data-driven, with ERP systems, analytics, automation, AI forecasting, and digital supply-chain platforms becoming important."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"2026–2030","text":"Foundation & Execution"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on becoming capable of independently handling operational supply-chain activities."},{"type":"h","text":"Core areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Procurement coordination"},{"text":"Inventory management"},{"text":"Logistics coordination"},{"text":"Warehouse operations"},{"text":"Production planning"},{"text":"Order management"},{"text":"Vendor coordination"},{"text":"Supply-demand tracking"},{"text":"ERP usage"},{"text":"Excel and Power BI"},{"text":"Basic supply-chain analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Likely entry roles:"},{"type":"lis