ger"},{"text":"Head of Supply Chain"},{"text":"Head of Planning"},{"text":"Supply Chain Director"},{"text":"Operations Director"},{"text":"Supply Chain Transformation Leader"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Progression depends heavily on industry, company size, leadership ability, and specialization."}]},{"heading":"Year-Wise UG Learning Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Engineering & Business Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Basic programming"},{"text":"Engineering economics"},{"text":"Introduction to industrial engineering"},{"text":"Basic operations management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft Excel"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Basic SQL"},{"text":"Basic Python"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Excel topics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"IF functions"},{"text":"SUMIFS/COUNTIFS"},{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Data cleaning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Outcome"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a foundation in quantitative analysis and business operations."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Operations & Supply Chain Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Supply Chain"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Purchasing"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Warehousing"},{"text":"Transportation"},{"text":"Distribution"},{"text":"Order fulfillment"},{"text":"Supplier management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Industrial Engineering"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Work study"},{"text":"Time study"},{"text":"Method study"},{"text":"Facility planning"},{"text":"Capacity planning"},{"text":"Production planning"},{"text":"Operations research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative methods"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linear programming"},{"text":"Transportation models"},{"text":"Assignment problems"},{"text":"Queuing theory"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Inventory models"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an Inventory Optimization Model using Excel."},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SKU demand"},{"text":"Lead time"},{"text":"Safety stock"},{"text":"Reorder point"},{"text":"EOQ"},{"text":"Stock-out risk"},{"text":"Inventory carrying cost"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Advanced Supply Chain & Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on practical business systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Planning"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Demand planning"},{"text":"Supply planning"},{"text":"Material Requirements Planning"},{"text":"Production scheduling"},{"text":"Capacity planning"},{"text":"S&OP"},{"text":"Distribution requirements planning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Procurement"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RFQ/RFP"},{"text":"Supplier evaluation"},{"text":"Vendor negotiation"},{"text":"Purchase orders"},{"text":"Supplier performance"},{"text":"Procurement analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Logistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transportation planning"},{"text":"Route optimization"},{"text":"Freight management"},{"text":"Distribution networks"},{"text":"3PL management"},{"text":"Last-mile logistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn at least one major ERP ecosystem:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SAP"},{"text":"Oracle"},{"text":"Microsoft Dynamics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For students targeting manufacturing, SAP exposure is particularly useful."}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Analytics, ERP & Industry Application","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus on becoming employable rather than studying only theory."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced tools"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Power BI","SQL","Python","ERP"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Power Pivot"},{"text":"DAX basics"},{"text":"SQL joins"},{"text":"SQL aggregations"},{"text":"Python pandas"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Dashboard development"},{"text":"ERP workflows"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Supply Chain KPIs"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Inventory turnover"},{"text":"Days Inventory Outstanding"},{"text":"OTIF"},{"text":"Fill rate"},{"text":"Service level"},{"text":"Stock-out rate"},{"text":"Forecast accuracy"},{"text":"Supplier lead time"},{"text":"Purchase price variance"},{"text":"Order cycle time"},{"text":"Warehouse utilization"},{"text":"Logistics cost per unit"}]}]},{"heading":"Important Supply Chain Workflows","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A student should understand the complete:"},{"type":"h","text":"Procure-to-Pay"},{"type":"flow","items":["Supplier selection","RFQ","Purchase Order","Goods Receipt","Invoice","Payment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Order-to-Delivery"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customer Order","Inventory Check","Production/Procurement","Warehouse","Transportation","Customer Delivery"]},{"type":"h","text":"Plan-to-Produce"},{"type":"flow","items":["Demand Forecast","Production Plan","Material Requirement","Procurement","Production","Finished Goods","Distribution"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding these workflows is often more valuable than memorizing definitions."}]},{"heading":"Technology Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Recommended Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Spreadsheet"},{"text":"Advanced Excel"}],[{"text":"Visualization"},{"text":"Power BI"}],[{"text":"Database"},{"text":"SQL"}],[{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Python"}],[{"text":"ERP"},{"text":"SAP / Oracle / Dynamics"}],[{"text":"Analytics"},{"text":"Pandas, statistics"}],[{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"Time-series forecasting"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"PowerPoint, process mapping"}],[{"text":"Process improvement"},{"text":"Lean, Six Sigma"}],[{"text":"